<slide>
  footer: off
</slide>

<h2>This slide has no footer</h2>

<p>
  <c>footer: off</c> in the <c><slide></c> block hides the bar for one slide, for example in front of a full-screen demo.
  The bar fades out and the built-in slide counter comes back. The space stays reserved, so nothing on the slide moves when a bar appears or disappears.
</p>

<notes>
  Same for header: off.
</notes>
